<tr><td colspan=4><font size=2 face=verdana color=#ffffff>Hail to thee friends! Pull up a stump, sip from a bottle of some fine Elven wine, and hear the tales of Keiden's adventures.<p>
Born in a far off land called Elanthia, Keiden was always a curious lad, seeking knowledge, and always searching for an adventure. As the eldest son of the Alustre'el clan of wood elves, he followed in the footsteps of his father and trained in the ways of a ranger and in the art of fletching.<p>
At an early age Keiden set out to explore the world and find adventure, traveling to many different parts of the world, meeting and sometimes battling many strange creatures and races. Being a ranger and spending most his time outside of cities, Keiden never built up much wealth, he preferred to forage for what he needed as he needed it, and not stockpile as other folks may.<p>
One day Keiden happened across a rather large person crouched in the hollowed out section of a large tree. At first he thought the person to be human, as he had rounded ears instead of the pointy ears common to elves, but the man seemed much much to large to be a human. Keiden creeped closer and closer to the tree, the man was not moving, nor making a sound. Keiden thought to himself "could he be dead?"<p>
Keiden unsheathed his sword and crept closer, slowly he reached out and poked the man in the arm with the sword. The man didn't move. Keiden stepped closer and poked the man again, still nothing. Keiden thought to himself, the poor man must be dead, sheathed his sword again, and stepped closer to pull the man from the tree and give him proper burial.<p>
As Keiden reached grasping range, the giant man sprang from the tree and grabbed him around the neck. "You thieving elves!" the man shouted, "I'll teach you a lesson you'll not soon forget!"<p>
"Please don't kill me sir" Keiden said. "I merely thought you had gone with your god, you didn't move when I poked at you and I was merely going to remove you from the tree and give you burial so the animals did not eat you."<p>
The man shouted again "Would you move if someone was poking at you with a sword? You should have spoken and made your presence known!"<p>
Keiden apologized to the man, and asked him to release him from his grasp, and the man did so. Keiden then said "You don't seem to have many supplies stranger, and you look hungry, would you care to share my food with me tonight?"<p>
The man replied "It has been a couple days since I have eaten, my name is Karlaor and I would be most grateful to you for some food and water."So Keiden and Karlaor sat down to eat together and conversed further.<p>
Keiden asked "Aren't you a rather large human?"<p>
Karlaor replied "If I was a mere human, I would be considered large, but among my people I am considered quite small."<p>
Keiden asked "And just who are your people?"<p>
Karlaor replied "I am a Barbarian!, I am from the far north and traveling south to catch the ship heading for the new world!"<p>
Keiden asked "The new world? What new world?"<p>
Karlaor then explained that he was heading for a new world recently discovered called Britannia, and explained how he had come to be in the tree trunk with no food or water. Keiden and Karlaor agreed to travel together to the south and headed off the next morning on their new adventures together.<p>
The two travelers had many adventures together along their journey, and had saved each others lives so often that they had become the best of friends. They visited many strange lands before reaching their final destination of Britannia, and had bonded so much that they started considering each other as brothers, and Karlaor started using Keiden's surname because he had none of his own, barbarians didn't use surnames.<p>
Several years passed by and the pair was getting the urge to seek new adventure in other strange new lands, when they heard of a new land called Derreth, so they headed off to the closest city with shipping docks to seek passage to Derreth.<p>
The journey to Derreth was long, and after arriving and spending several months there, they still could not find the adventure they were seeking. When they overheard a stranger in a tavern one night speak of another new land called Norrath, they heard the stranger speak of many strange creatures they had not heard of before, and even speak of wood elves and barbarians, and it had been such a long time since they had seen any others of their kind, that they knew this new land was the place for them. So they set off together again for the new land called Norrath.<p>
Upon arriving in Norrath, they both agreed to go their own way and to seek their own people, and to meet up again at a later time. Karlaor headed off to the north, knowing that if this strange new land really had barbarians, then he would find them in the cold north where they like to live, and Keiden set off to find the largest forest he could, knowing his wood elf brethren love to be among the trees and animals of a forest.<p>
Keiden finally found his forest, and his people. In a forest called Faydark, and a city called Kelethin, and he has found a home in the Norrath Militia.<p>
OOC Summary:<p>
I have been playing online RPGs for several years.Starting in the MUD called Gemstone III, set in the world of Elanthia, ending up here in EverQuest in the world of Norrath. For those that don't know of these other worlds I mentioned, I have listed below what games they go with if I know myself, hehe.<p>
Elanthia: Gemstone III and DragonRealms<br>
Britannia: Ultima Online<br>
Derreth: Asheron's Call<p>
All the strange lands I mentioned are various games I have played but never knew the correct name of the world, those games are listed below.<p>
Meridian 59<br>
The Realm<br>
Pantera<p>
I am by no means a "true" role-player by any sense of the term. I do try, and there are times you will see me in game speaking in the elvish tongue, but most of the time I have to use common tongue or people won't answer my questions, even if they can understand elvish.as for Karlaor, that is my barbarian warrior character, just thought tying him into the story might be kind of cool, heh.<p>
And though I am not at lvl 20 and can't add a surname in game, the one I have listed on web site is the one I plan to use.<p>
Glad to be a part of the guild, and hope to see more of you do background stories on yourselves and your characters.<p>

Keiden Alustre'el the wood elf<br>
Ranger of the 10th season<p>&nbsp;</font></td></tr>

